      "text": "Day 3 · A tour of the historic inner city of Paramaribo, a UNESCO World Heritage Site famous for its buildings of hard tropical wood: Independence Square, the Palm Garden, the waterfront, the Central and Maroon markets, and the cathedral basilica, mosque and synagogue standing side by side. Then the former coffee plantation of Peperpot, now a nature park where wildlife has reclaimed the land, and a boat ride back to Paramaribo from Nieuw Amsterdam, watching for Guiana dolphins in the Suriname River. (B)",
